WEBVTT

00:00:04.639 --> 00:00:09.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Tuesday the sixth. Can you all hear me over that fan?</v>

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:15.400
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, just. Sorry I'm a bit flustered, traffic on the ring road was absolutely ridiculous.</v>

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.239
<v Tomasz Nowak>So, normal traffic on the ring road, then?</v>

00:00:20.679 --> 00:00:24.879
<v Hannah Price>Pretty much. Had ages to look at the same bloke's brake lights.</v>

00:00:26.579 --> 00:00:30.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Well, there's a birthday cake in the office, if that improves things.</v>

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:36.280
<v Grace Liu>Depends. Proper cake or one of those healthy ones?</v>

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.390
<v Sarah Okafor>Proper cake. Right, before this becomes the cake meeting—what's already closed out? Atlas?</v>

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:47.939
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I already swapped the filter on the Atlas yesterday. That's done.</v>

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:53.380
<v Grace Liu>And I tested the Atlas yesterday and it's all fine now.</v>

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:59.250
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, you both came through together a bit. Filter changed and tested, both finished?</v>

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.640
<v Grace Liu>Both finished, yeah. Nothing outstanding from that test.</v>

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.489
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Closed, not another job for today.</v>

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:17.219
<v Fiona Doyle>Only an observation from me: noticed the Water Booster Pump was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:20.530
<v Tomasz Nowak>Settled while it was still running, you mean?</v>

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:25.670
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah. Not raising a job off it, just passing on what nights said.</v>

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.760
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, observation only.</v>

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:36.000
<v Aisha Begum>Um, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the 11kV board. Same blocker as before.</v>

00:01:37.829 --> 00:01:41.329
<v Fiona Doyle>So there's still no confirmed delivery to put against it?</v>

00:01:41.989 --> 00:01:47.239
<v Aisha Begum>No. Still blocked, no change. I'm not announcing a date or a new action there.</v>

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:53.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. And the shutdown on the power pack on one is cancelled now, production need it running.</v>

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:58.879
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, cancelled altogether, not just moved a few hours?</v>

00:02:00.569 --> 00:02:04.420
<v Sarah Okafor>Cancelled. No shutdown work on that coming out of this meeting.</v>

00:02:06.409 --> 00:02:07.609
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep, clear.</v>

00:02:08.939 --> 00:02:13.840
<v Sarah Okafor>Tommo, can you schedule downtime for the turbine two with production, by next Tuesday?</v>

00:02:14.629 --> 00:02:21.629
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah—just to be clear, you want the downtime arranged by next Tuesday, not me assuming that's the actual outage day?</v>

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:28.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Agree the downtime with production by next Tuesday. We're not fixing the outage day on this call.</v>

00:02:29.289 --> 00:02:33.840
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, I'll schedule downtime for the turbine two with production by next Tuesday.</v>

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:41.090
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, better than us putting a slot in and calling it agreed when it isn't.</v>

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:45.979
<v Tomasz Nowak>Quite. A coloured square isn't permission, much as we'd like it to be.</v>

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:51.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Fi, can you do the pre-use checks on the counterbalances? Top priority please.</v>

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:58.419
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, I'll do the pre-use checks on the counterbalances. That's my top priority.</v>

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:04.949
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, pre-use being the important bit there. Not paperwork after they've already been used.</v>

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.780
<v Fiona Doyle>Absolutely. Checks before use, understood.</v>

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:14.539
<v Sarah Okafor>Next, spares. Can you order spare parts for the little water valve on two? Next week, no rush.</v>

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:22.770
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Me? Sorry, no, I can't take that one on. I haven't got the capacity for the ordering as well.</v>

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:30.169
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Ash, can you take that instead—order spare parts for the little water valve on two next week? No rush.</v>

00:03:32.469 --> 00:03:38.770
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I'll take it instead. I'll order spare parts for the little water valve on two next week.</v>

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.439
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Cheers. And that's not suddenly an urgent one because it's changed hands?</v>

00:03:45.789 --> 00:03:48.590
<v Sarah Okafor>No, same as before. No rush, next week.</v>

00:03:50.419 --> 00:03:52.169
<v Aisha Begum>Fine by me. That's clear.</v>

00:03:53.750 --> 00:04:01.449
<v Sarah Okafor>We've also got the shift handover report to send round. Whenever you get a chance sort of thing, not an urgent one.</v>

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.699
<v Grace Liu>I'll send the shift handover report round.</v>

00:04:06.289 --> 00:04:08.740
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace. Whenever you get a chance.</v>

00:04:09.979 --> 00:04:13.479
<v Grace Liu>Yep, understood. Not putting it ahead of the priority checks.</v>

00:04:14.069 --> 00:04:18.970
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, did you say the test report or the shift handover report? Audio clipped.</v>

00:04:20.569 --> 00:04:24.769
<v Grace Liu>Shift handover report. The Atlas test is finished, that wasn't another action.</v>

00:04:25.449 --> 00:04:30.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Doyler, can you investigate the pressure drop on the line one HPU by Monday?</v>

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:36.899
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep. Fi for the checks, Doyler for the pressure drop. Sadly still only one of me.</v>

00:04:38.689 --> 00:04:43.589
<v Sarah Okafor>I know, the budget won't stretch to a second one. Monday for that investigation.</v>

00:04:44.079 --> 00:04:50.730
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay, I'll investigate the pressure drop on the line one HPU by Monday. The counterbalances checks stay top priority.</v>

00:04:53.029 --> 00:04:56.879
<v Tomasz Nowak>Investigation only at this point, yeah? Not agreeing a strip-down here?</v>

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:03.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct, investigate the pressure drop. We're not adding a strip-down to it.</v>

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.000
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, that's what I've got.</v>

00:05:07.149 --> 00:05:11.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you chase the purchase order for the desiccant unit by 11am?</v>

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:16.680
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll chase the purchase order for the desiccant unit by 11am.</v>

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:22.540
<v Aisha Begum>And that's separate from my supplier delivery blocker, just so we don't muddle the two?</v>

00:05:23.319 --> 00:05:29.269
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, separate. The 11kV board is still blocked; this is the purchase order for the desiccant unit.</v>

00:05:30.139 --> 00:05:35.740
<v Hannah Price>Got it. Chase by 11am, not a promise that the order will be released by then.</v>

00:05:36.959 --> 00:05:41.160
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. That's the six actions covered, and the cancelled shutdown stays cancelled.</v>

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:48.209
<v Olumide Adeyemi>That last bit came through beautifully. Teams apparently likes us more at the end.</v>

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.540
<v Tomasz Nowak>Either that or the fan's finally stopped competing with you.</v>

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:57.000
<v Hannah Price>I heard cake perfectly at the start, to be fair.</v>

00:05:59.259 --> 00:06:01.360
<v Grace Liu>Selective hearing. Very common engineering condition.</v>

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:05.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, on that highly technical note, thanks everyone. End there.</v>
